---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { affiliateTag } from "../lib/site";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Disclosure"
  description="FTC affiliate disclosure for Oli's Bookshelf. Amazon Associates is not active yet."
>
  <header class="page-head">
    <p class="eyebrow">Money and links</p>
    <h1>Disclosure</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      This page is the full affiliate and advertising disclosure. If a later post mentions a retailer,
      this is still the controlling text until we replace it.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="disclosure-box">
    <p style="margin:0 0 0.6rem;">
      <strong>As an Amazon Associate I earn from qualifying purchases.</strong>
    </p>
    <p class="small" style="margin:0;">
      That sentence is here to meet Amazon’s required Associates wording. The program is
      <strong>not active yet</strong>. We have not applied, we have not been approved, and we have
      not put a live Associates tag on this site.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>What that means today</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Book search links use the public placeholder tag <code>{affiliateTag}</code>. They are not
        meant to generate commission.
      </li>
      <li>We do not claim income, traffic, or “this niche prints money.”</li>
      <li>
        If Associates is approved later, we will replace the placeholder, keep this disclosure, and
        note the change date in the repository.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>FTC note</h2>
    <p>
      If a link on this site could earn a commission in the future, we will say so on the page and
      keep this disclosure linked from the footer. We do not accept paid placements for reading-order
      facts. A retailer paying for a ranking would be a review, and we do not publish reviews.
    </p>

    <h2>What we will not do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Hide a live tag behind a “just a search link” label</li>
      <li>Invent testimonials about products</li>
      <li>Promise that buying through us funds the site in any specific amount</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      More detail lives in <code>docs/HOW_IT_EARNS.md</code>.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
